      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect. According to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through **credential injection at spawn time**:\n\n1. **Secrets are loaded externally**: A local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup.\n\n2. **Injection only into child processes**: The key is injected directly into the environment of spawned child processes (the Ingest agent and Query agent) \u2014 *immediately before they start* \u2014 rather than being written into the Hub\u0027s own process environment.\n\n3. **Hub\u0027s environment never mutated**: The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never modified to include the credential.\n\nThis design isolates the credential from the Hub itself: even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the API key simply by reading its own environment variables, because the key was never there in the first place. The credential exists only in the short-lived child processes that actually need it to call the Anthropic API.",
